                    <h1 class="content-title">Continuous Monitoring & <span class="gradient-text">Control Testing</span></h1>
                    <p class="content-subtitle">
                        Move from periodic, manual compliance checks to automated, real-time monitoring. 
                        Understand indicators, attestation workflows, CCM, AI-powered risk management with 
                        Now Assist, and how to build dashboards that keep your risk posture visible.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <!-- Why Continuous Monitoring -->
                <section class="content-section" id="why-continuous">
                    <h2>Why Continuous Monitoring?</h2>
                    <p>
                        Traditional GRC operated on a <strong>periodic assessment model</strong> — controls were 
                        tested once a quarter or once a year, and the organization operated blind between assessments. 
                        A control could fail on Day 2 and not be discovered until Day 90 at the next audit cycle.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        <strong>Continuous Monitoring</strong> closes this gap by automating data collection and 
                        validation in real time. Instead of asking "Was this control effective last quarter?", 
                        the system answers "Is this control effective <em>right now</em>?" — and alerts you 
                        immediately when it isn't.
                    </p>

                    <div class="table-responsive">
                        <table class="styled-table">
                            <thead>
                                <tr>
                                    <th>Approach</th>
                                    <th>Periodic (Traditional)</th>
                                    <th>Continuous (IRM)</th>
                                </tr>
                            </thead>
                            <tbody>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>Testing Frequency</strong></td>
                                    <td>Quarterly / Annually</td>
                                    <td>Daily / Real-time</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>Detection Time</strong></td>
                                    <td>Weeks to months</td>
                                    <td>Minutes to hours</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>Evidence Quality</strong></td>
                                    <td>Self-reported, point-in-time</td>
                                    <td>System-generated, continuous</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>Audit Readiness</strong></td>
                                    <td>Requires manual preparation</td>
                                    <td>Always audit-ready</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>Resource Cost</strong></td>
                                    <td>High (manual effort each cycle)</td>
                                    <td>Lower after initial setup (automated)</td>
                                </tr>
                            </tbody>
                        </table>
                    </div>
                </section>

                <!-- Indicator Types -->
                <section class="content-section" id="indicator-types">
                    <h2>Indicator Types</h2>
                    <p>
                        <strong>Indicators</strong> are the backbone of continuous monitoring in ServiceNow IRM. 
                        They are automated checks that evaluate whether a control is operating effectively. 
                        When an indicator detects a deviation from the expected state, it can automatically 
                        flag the control as non-compliant and create remediation issues.
                    </p>

                    <h3>Three Types of Indicators</h3>
                    <div class="table-responsive">
                        <table class="styled-table">
                            <thead>
                                <tr>
                                    <th>Type</th>
                                    <th>How It Works</th>
                                    <th>Use Case</th>
                                    <th>Effort</th>
                                </tr>
                            </thead>
                            <tbody>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>Manual Indicator</strong></td>
                                    <td>A human reviews evidence and manually sets the indicator result (Pass/Fail)</td>
                                    <td>Physical security checks, procedural reviews, qualitative assessments</td>
                                    <td>High (requires human judgment each cycle)</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>Automated Indicator</strong></td>
                                    <td>Queries a ServiceNow table and evaluates the result against a threshold (e.g., "count of unpatched servers < 5")</td>
                                    <td>CMDB checks, configuration compliance, SLA monitoring</td>
                                    <td>Low (set-and-forget after configuration)</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>Scripted Indicator</strong></td>
                                    <td>Runs a custom server-side script that performs complex logic and returns a Pass/Fail result</td>
                                    <td>Multi-table validation, cross-system checks, complex business logic</td>
                                    <td>Medium (requires development and testing)</td>
                                </tr>
                            </tbody>
                        </table>
                    </div>

                    <div class="diagram-block">
                        <div class="diagram-title">Indicator Execution Flow</div>
                        <div class="mermaid">
                        flowchart LR
                            A["Scheduled Job<br/>(Nightly Run)"] --> B["Execute<br/>Indicator"]
                            B --> C{"Result?"}
                            C -->|"Pass"| D["Update Control<br/>Status: Compliant"]
                            C -->|"Fail"| E["Update Control<br/>Status: Non-Compliant"]
                            E --> F["Auto-Create<br/>Issue"]
                            F --> G["Assign to<br/>Control Owner"]
                            D --> H["Log Evidence<br/>& Timestamp"]
                            E --> H

                            style A fill:transparent,stroke:#6b7280,color:#d1d5db
                            style B fill:transparent,stroke:#3b82f6,color:#d1d5db
                            style C fill:transparent,stroke:#8b5cf6,color:#d1d5db
                            style D fill:transparent,stroke:#10b981,color:#d1d5db
                            style E fill:transparent,stroke:#ef4444,color:#d1d5db
                            style F fill:transparent,stroke:#f59e0b,color:#d1d5db
                            style G fill:transparent,stroke:#f59e0b,color:#d1d5db
                            style H fill:transparent,stroke:#06b6d4,color:#d1d5db
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="info-card info-card--warning">
                        <div class="info-card-title">Indicator Limitations</div>
                        <p>
                            Indicators are <strong>not weighted</strong> — they are evaluated equally when 
                            calculating a control's overall compliance status. If you need weighted impact 
                            (e.g., a critical security indicator should matter more than a documentation check), 
                            you must handle that logic separately through custom scoring models or Risk 
                            Assessment Methodology (RAM) configuration.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </section>

                <!-- Attestation Workflows -->
                <section class="content-section" id="attestation">
                    <h2>Attestation Workflows</h2>
                    <p>
                        <strong>Attestation</strong> is the periodic, survey-based process where control owners 
                        manually confirm that controls are implemented and operating effectively. While continuous 
                        monitoring automates many checks, attestation remains essential for controls that require 
                        human judgment.
                    </p>

                    <h3>Attestation Lifecycle</h3>
                    <div class="diagram-block">
                        <div class="diagram-title">Attestation Cycle</div>
                        <div class="mermaid">
                        flowchart LR
                            A["Generate<br/>Attestation"] --> B["Assign to<br/>Control Owner"]
                            B --> C["Owner Reviews<br/>Control Evidence"]
                            C --> D{"Attestation<br/>Result"}
                            D -->|"Effective"| E["Control Status:<br/>Compliant"]
                            D -->|"Ineffective"| F["Create Issue<br/>& Remediate"]
                            D -->|"N/A"| G["Mark as<br/>Not Applicable"]

                            style A fill:transparent,stroke:#3b82f6,color:#d1d5db
                            style B fill:transparent,stroke:#8b5cf6,color:#d1d5db
                            style C fill:transparent,stroke:#f59e0b,color:#d1d5db
                            style D fill:transparent,stroke:#6b7280,color:#d1d5db
                            style E fill:transparent,stroke:#10b981,color:#d1d5db
                            style F fill:transparent,stroke:#ef4444,color:#d1d5db
                            style G fill:transparent,stroke:#6b7280,color:#d1d5db
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <h3>Attestation vs Automated Testing</h3>
                    <div class="table-responsive">
                        <table class="styled-table">
                            <thead>
                                <tr>
                                    <th>Aspect</th>
                                    <th>Attestation</th>
                                    <th>Automated Testing</th>
                                </tr>
                            </thead>
                            <tbody>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>How</strong></td>
                                    <td>Survey sent to control owner</td>
                                    <td>Script/query executed by system</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>Frequency</strong></td>
                                    <td>Quarterly / Semi-annually</td>
                                    <td>Daily / Real-time</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>Best For</strong></td>
                                    <td>Procedural controls, physical security, governance</td>
                                    <td>Technical controls, configuration checks, data validation</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>Evidence</strong></td>
                                    <td>Human-verified, includes context and judgment</td>
                                    <td>System-generated, objective and repeatable</td>
                                </tr>
                            </tbody>
                        </table>
                    </div>
                </section>

                <!-- Continuous Control Monitoring -->
                <section class="content-section" id="ccm">
                    <h2>Continuous Control Monitoring (CCM)</h2>
                    <p>
                        <strong>CCM</strong> combines indicators and automated testing into a unified framework 
                        that provides real-time visibility into the effectiveness of your entire control environment.
                    </p>

                    <h3>CCM Components</h3>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Control Tests</strong> — Scheduled or event-driven tests that validate specific control attributes.</li>
                        <li><strong>Threshold Monitoring</strong> — Alerts triggered when metrics cross predefined thresholds (e.g., > 10 unresolved vulnerabilities on a critical server).</li>
                        <li><strong>Trend Analysis</strong> — Performance Analytics tracks control effectiveness over time, identifying degradation trends before they become failures.</li>
                        <li><strong>Automated Issue Creation</strong> — When a control test fails, the system automatically creates a GRC Issue linked to the control and assigns it to the control owner.</li>
                        <li><strong>Evidence Collection</strong> — Each test execution generates timestamped evidence records, maintaining a continuous audit trail.</li>
                    </ul>

                    <div class="info-card info-card--tip">
                        <div class="info-card-title">Scheduled Job: GRC Indicator Nightly Run</div>
                        <p>
                            The <code>GRC indicator nightly run</code> is the out-of-the-box Scheduled Job that 
                            executes all active indicators. It runs by default at 2:00 AM server time. If your 
                            indicators aren't producing results, the first troubleshooting step is to verify 
                            this job is active and running successfully. Check: <strong>System Definition → 
                            Scheduled Jobs → GRC indicator nightly run</strong>.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </section>

